          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-pullback
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} limit in an (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of the shape
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo ←
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{a \to c \leftarrow b\} \to \mathcal{C}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In other words it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi C
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A \times_C B &amp;\to&amp; B
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\cong\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  A &amp;\to&amp; C
                  }
          %p
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            among all such cones in the
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            This is the analog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %h2#incarnations Incarnations
          %h3#in_quasicategories In quasi-categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limit in a quasi-category
          %p
            The non-degenerate cells of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1] \times \Delta[1]
            obtained as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of the simplicial 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            with itself look like
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (0,0) &amp;\to&amp; (1,0)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\searrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  (0,1) &amp;\to&amp; (1,1)
                  }
          %p
            A
            %strong square
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an image of this in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  s : \Delta[1] \times \Delta[1] \to C
                  \\,.
          %p
            The simplicial square
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]^{\times 2}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+simplicial+sets"} join of simplicial sets
            of a 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            with the point:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
