            %p
              We could also prove this by showing that this functor is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+final+functor"} homotopy initial
              using the characterization in terms of slice categories, and then invoking the theorem of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HTT"} HTT
              4.1.1.3(4) which says (in dual form) that an inclusion of simplicial sets is homotopy initial if and only if it is left anodyne.
            %p
              One of the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/right%2Fleft+Kan+fibration#PropRightAnodyne"} properties of left anodyne morphisms
              is that restriction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-categories"} over quasi-categories
              along left anodyne morphisms produces an acyclic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is also an acyclic fibration observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              can be factored as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,f)} \leftarrow
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,e,f)} \leftarrow
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(b,c,d,e,f)}
            %p
              Observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,e,f)}\leftarrow\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(b,c,d,e,f)}
              fits into a pullback diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mi d
                                %mo ,
                                %mi e
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi b
                                %mo ,
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mi d
                                %mo ,
                                %mi e
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mi e
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi b
                                %mo ,
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mi e
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,e,f)}
                    \&amp; \leftarrow &amp;
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(b,c,d,e,f)} \\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,e,f)}
                    \&amp; \leftarrow &amp;
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(b,c,e,f)}
                    }
            %p
              and hence is an acyclic Kan fibration since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,e,f)} \leftarrow \mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(b,c,e,f)}
              is one, on account of the fact that the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\sigma(b) &amp; \to &amp; \sigma(c) \\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\
                    \\sigma(e) &amp; \to &amp; \sigma(f)
                    }
            %p
              is a pullback in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,f)} \leftarrow \mathcal{C}_{/\sigma(c,d,e,f)}
              is a trivial fibration since
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi c
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi d
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo →
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi f
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi c
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi d
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo →
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi e
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo →
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi f
                              %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; &amp; c \\
                    \&amp; &amp; \downarrow \\
                    d &amp; \to &amp; f
                    }
                    \\right) &amp; \to &amp;
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; c \\
                    \&amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \downarrow \\
                    d &amp; \to &amp; e &amp; \to &amp; f
                    }
                    \\right)
                    }
            %p
              is left anodyne; clearly this is a pushout of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi e
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d\to f)\to (d\to e\to f)
              and so it suffices to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{\{0,2\}}\to \Delta^{\{0,1,2\}}
              is left anodyne. But this map factors as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 0
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{\{0,2\}}\to \Lambda^2_0 \to \Delta^{\{0,1,2\}}
              and clearly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 0
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{\{0,2\}}\to \Lambda^2_0
              is left anodyne since it is a pushout of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Delta^{\{0\}}\to
                      \\Delta^{\{0,1\}}
          %h3#in_model_categories In model categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          %h3#in_derivators In derivators
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+in+a+derivator"} pullback in a derivator
          %h3#in_simplicial_type_theory In simplicial type theory
          %h4#for_segal_types For Segal types
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type+theory"} simplicial type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+types"} Segal types
            are the types that represent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precategory+objects+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-precategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a type in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type+theory"} simplicial type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z:A
            be three elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathrm{hom}_A(x, z)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:\mathrm{hom}_A(y, z)
            be two morphisms. The
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-pullback
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is an tuple consisting of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an element
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ×
                          %mi z
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times_z^{f,g} y:A
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} outl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ×
                          %mi z
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{outl}(f, g):\mathrm{hom}_A(x \times_z^{f,g} y, x)
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
